id: pm-o7u08u
title: Agent-task gate accepts incidental substrings as required-field completeness
description: "Greptile review on PR #1133 found that the mandatory agent-task token gate serializes the whole payload and searches for required-field text. Generic names such as code or recovery can therefore be satisfied by unrelated nested keys or message values. Make required_fields explicit dot-separated own-property paths, update the golden corpus to describe structural consumption, and prove misleading substring payloads fail."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:ci","area:sdk",completeness,review-feedback
created_at: "2026-08-27T17:58:02.801Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T07:52:20.228Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T07:52:19.672Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T07:52:19.672Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Every required_fields entry is resolved as an own-property path from the output root; Incidental keys and string values cannot satisfy completeness; The golden corpus uses structural paths for entity and mutation outputs; Exact unit, transcript replay, and full coverage gates pass"
parent: pm-8pnj
resolution: "completed: completeness is evaluated on the exact projected public payload after accounting metadata is removed"
expected_result: Required transcript fields are proven by exact structural own-property paths rather than incidental serialized text.
actual_result: "validateAgentTaskTokenInvocation now resolves required_fields against independentlyProjectedPayload, the same value validated and reported; token_accounting.total_bytes cannot certify projected completeness."
